    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All green \u2014 full build succeeds with 47 acceptance tests passing (including the new `Cp34Tests`) and no regressions.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `birthDate` intake and derived `ageBand` for `POST /api/owners` (read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`), computed against `registrationDate`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added optional `birthDate` (ISO date) to the `OwnerFields` schema, and a read-only `ageBand` string to the `Owner` schema. These regenerate `OwnerFieldsDto.birthDate` and `OwnerDto.ageBand`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps the request's `birthDate` onto the entity.\n\n3. **`AgeBand.java`** (new mapper helper) \u2014 derives the band from `birthDate` measured against `registrationDate`: `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+); returns `null` (field absent) when no `birthDate` was supplied. Follows the existing `Locality`/`ContactPreference` helper pattern.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the read-time `@Mapping(target = \"ageBand\", expression = ...)`, matching how `checkDigit`, `membershipLevel`, etc. are derived.\n\n5. **DB schema** \u2014 added `birth_date DATE` to the `owners` table in all four dialect schemas (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres), and extended the hsqldb positional seed inserts by one `NULL` so the existing owner rows still load (the other dialects use named-column inserts and needed no change).\n\nThe derivation happens at read time in the mapper, consistent with the project's convention that DTO-derived fields live in mapper helpers rather than in the OfficeFloor pipeline steps.",
